        "WFPC2": "2026-11-05: blur set to 0 by hand after the auto-calibration disagreed with itself. F606W pass-1 chi^2 residual 0.753 det px rested on 5 marginal stars with a FLAT chi^2 landscape (flat-topped WFPC2 cores); applied to the twins it produced a 2.2x peak-flux deficit vs the real stars (median peak_frac 0.022 vs 0.051). At blur 0 the 22 S/N>=100 stars prefer no extra blur (FWHM ratios 0.51-0.84 i.e. real stars NARROWER than the model, peak-frac ratio 1.40 +/- 0.5): the MAST-DB model runs slightly wide for some fields, which is a model-error matter for psf_err, not fixable by blur>=0. F814W rested on 1 star. Revisit with a peak-flux-based calibrator if WFPC2 model width becomes a science question."
